<rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom" xmlns:s="https://wvusports.com/services/xml_schema/story" xmlns:media="http://search.yahoo.com/mrss/"><channel><title /><link>https://wvusports.com/rss/</link><description /><atom:link href="https://wvusports.com/rss" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml" /><language>en-us</language><ttl>60</ttl><item><title>WVU’s 2026 Big 12 Tournament Ends with PK Shootout</title><link>https://wvusports.com/news/2026/11/9/womens-soccer-wvus-2026-big-12-tournament-ends-with-pk-shootout</link><guid>https://wvusports.com/news/2026/11/9/womens-soccer-wvus-2026-big-12-tournament-ends-with-pk-shootout</guid><category>Women's Soccer</category><description><![CDATA[<img alt="Alexis Pashales dribbles down the field during the quarterfinals of the 2026 Big 12 Tournament." src="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_primary&image_path=/images/2026/11/9/Big_12_Tournament-4.jpg" /><br /><br />MANSFIELD, Texas – Despite a 90th minute goal to send the match into overtime, the No. 8-seeded West Virginia University women's soccer team played to a 1-1 draw with No. 1-seed BYU in double overtime. Following a penalty kick shootout to decide the advancing team, the Cougars won 4-2 to advance to the semifinals of the 2026 Big 12 Tournament inside Texas Health Mansfield Stadium in Mansfield, Texas, on Monday afternoon.]]></description><media:thumbnail url="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_system&amp;image_path=/images/2026/11/9/Big_12_Tournament-4.jpg" /><media:content url="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_primary&amp;image_path=/images/2026/11/9/Big_12_Tournament-4.jpg"><media:title>Alexis Pashales dribbles down the field during the quarterfinals of the 2026 Big 12 Tournament.</media:title></media:content><enclosure url="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_primary&amp;image_path=/images/2026/11/9/Big_12_Tournament-4.jpg" length="1" type="image/jpg" /><pubDate>Mon, 9 Nov 2026 19:27:00 EST</pubDate><s:sport_id>13</s:sport_id><s:story_id>59671</s:story_id></item><item><title>Forbes Named to Big 12 Starting Five</title><link>https://wvusports.com/news/2026/11/9/womens-basketball-forbes-named-to-big-12-starting-five</link><guid>https://wvusports.com/news/2026/11/9/womens-basketball-forbes-named-to-big-12-starting-five</guid><category>Women's Basketball</category><description><![CDATA[<img alt="Skylar Forbes drives to the hoop against George Washington" src="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_primary&image_path=/images/2026/11/9/WBBvsGeorgeWashington_Nov5_2026_AM_76.jpg" /><br /><br />MORGANTOWN, W.Va. – Following a standout three-game stretch to open the 2026-27 season, Skylar Forbes of West Virginia Women's Basketball has been named to the Big 12 Starting Five, the conference announced Monday.]]></description><media:thumbnail url="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_system&amp;image_path=/images/2026/11/9/WBBvsGeorgeWashington_Nov5_2026_AM_76.jpg" /><media:content url="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_primary&amp;image_path=/images/2026/11/9/WBBvsGeorgeWashington_Nov5_2026_AM_76.jpg"><media:title>Skylar Forbes drives to the hoop against George Washington</media:title></media:content><enclosure url="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_primary&amp;image_path=/images/2026/11/9/WBBvsGeorgeWashington_Nov5_2026_AM_76.jpg" length="1" type="image/jpg" /><pubDate>Mon, 9 Nov 2026 16:00:00 EST</pubDate><s:sport_id>9</s:sport_id><s:story_id>59667</s:story_id></item><item><title>Sadler Racks Up Big 12 Weekly Accolades</title><link>https://wvusports.com/news/2026/11/9/mens-basketball-sadler-racks-up-big-12-weekly-accolades</link><guid>https://wvusports.com/news/2026/11/9/mens-basketball-sadler-racks-up-big-12-weekly-accolades</guid><category>Men's Basketball</category><description><![CDATA[<img alt="Miles Sadler was named Big 12 Freshman of the Week & to Big 12 Starting 5" src="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_primary&image_path=/images/2026/11/9/MBB26_Big12WeeklyAward_1920x1080_MilesNov9.jpg" /><br /><br />IRVING, Texas - BYU's Robert Wright III earned Player of the Week while West Virginia's Miles Sadler earned Freshman of the Week honors in the first Monster Energy Big 12 Men's Basketball weekly awards of the 2026-27 season.]]></description><media:thumbnail url="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_system&amp;image_path=/images/2026/11/9/MBB26_Big12WeeklyAward_1920x1080_MilesNov9.jpg" /><media:content url="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_primary&amp;image_path=/images/2026/11/9/MBB26_Big12WeeklyAward_1920x1080_MilesNov9.jpg"><media:title>Miles Sadler was named Big 12 Freshman of the Week &amp; to Big 12 Starting 5</media:title></media:content><enclosure url="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_primary&amp;image_path=/images/2026/11/9/MBB26_Big12WeeklyAward_1920x1080_MilesNov9.jpg" length="1" type="image/jpg" /><pubDate>Mon, 9 Nov 2026 14:58:00 EST</pubDate><s:sport_id>4</s:sport_id><s:story_id>59670</s:story_id></item><item><title>Six-Day Window to be Exercised for Nov. 21 Houston Game</title><link>https://wvusports.com/news/2026/11/9/football-six-day-window-to-be-exercised-for-nov-21-houston-game</link><guid>https://wvusports.com/news/2026/11/9/football-six-day-window-to-be-exercised-for-nov-21-houston-game</guid><category>Football</category><description><![CDATA[<img alt="The backside of the North Endzone scoreboard at Milan Puskar Stadium. " src="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_primary&image_path=/images/2026/8/12/videoboard.jpg" /><br /><br />MORGANTOWN, W.Va. (November 9, 2026) – The Big 12 Conference has announced that ESPN and FOX will utilize a six-day window to announce the broadcast network and time slot for WVU's Saturday, Nov. 21 Big 12 Conference football game against No. 14/16 Houston, as presented by the West Virginia Lottery, at Milan Puskar Stadim.]]></description><media:thumbnail url="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_system&amp;image_path=/images/2026/8/12/videoboard.jpg" /><media:content url="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_primary&amp;image_path=/images/2026/8/12/videoboard.jpg"><media:title>The backside of the North Endzone scoreboard at Milan Puskar Stadium. </media:title></media:content><enclosure url="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_primary&amp;image_path=/images/2026/8/12/videoboard.jpg" length="1" type="image/jpg" /><pubDate>Mon, 9 Nov 2026 12:43:00 EST</pubDate><s:sport_id>2</s:sport_id><s:story_id>59668</s:story_id></item><item><title>Shivers Named Student-Athlete of the Week</title><link>https://wvusports.com/news/2026/11/9/golf-shivers-named-student-athlete-of-the-week</link><guid>https://wvusports.com/news/2026/11/9/golf-shivers-named-student-athlete-of-the-week</guid><category>Golf</category><description><![CDATA[<img alt="Michael Shivers watches his shot at the Pearl at Kalauoa Invitational" src="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_primary&image_path=/images/2026/11/9/Pearl_At_Kalauao_3rd_Rd_-1.jpg" /><br /><br />MORGANTOWN, W.Va. – Freshman Michael Shivers of the West Virginia University golf team has been named the WVU Student-Athlete of the Week, presented by University Apartments.]]></description><media:thumbnail url="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_system&amp;image_path=/images/2026/11/9/Pearl_At_Kalauao_3rd_Rd_-1.jpg" /><media:content url="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_primary&amp;image_path=/images/2026/11/9/Pearl_At_Kalauao_3rd_Rd_-1.jpg"><media:title>Michael Shivers watches his shot at the Pearl at Kalauoa Invitational</media:title></media:content><enclosure url="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_primary&amp;image_path=/images/2026/11/9/Pearl_At_Kalauao_3rd_Rd_-1.jpg" length="1" type="image/jpg" /><pubDate>Mon, 9 Nov 2026 12:27:00 EST</pubDate><s:sport_id>5</s:sport_id><s:story_id>59669</s:story_id></item><item><title>Mountaineers Cruise Past Georgia Southern in Sun Belt Quarterfinals</title><link>https://wvusports.com/news/2026/11/8/mens-soccer-mountaineers-cruise-past-georgia-southern-in-sun-belt-quarterfinals</link><guid>https://wvusports.com/news/2026/11/8/mens-soccer-mountaineers-cruise-past-georgia-southern-in-sun-belt-quarterfinals</guid><category>Men's Soccer</category><description><![CDATA[<img alt="Men's Soccer celebrates after scoring a goal" src="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_primary&image_path=/images/2026/11/9/MSOC_vsGeorgiaSouthern_Nov8_2026_AM-45.jpg" /><br /><br />MORGANTOWN, W.Va. – The No. 9 West Virginia University men's soccer team rolled to a 4-0 victory over Georgia Southern in the Sun Belt quarterfinals, Sunday afternoon at Dick Dlesk Soccer Stadium. The top-seeded Mountaineers improve to 11-2-4 overall and advance to the semifinals against the winner between James Madison and Coastal Carolina.]]></description><media:thumbnail url="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_system&amp;image_path=/images/2026/11/9/MSOC_vsGeorgiaSouthern_Nov8_2026_AM-45.jpg" /><media:content url="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_primary&amp;image_path=/images/2026/11/9/MSOC_vsGeorgiaSouthern_Nov8_2026_AM-45.jpg"><media:title>Men's Soccer celebrates after scoring a goal</media:title></media:content><enclosure url="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_primary&amp;image_path=/images/2026/11/9/MSOC_vsGeorgiaSouthern_Nov8_2026_AM-45.jpg" length="1" type="image/jpg" /><pubDate>Sun, 8 Nov 2026 20:44:00 EST</pubDate><s:sport_id>6</s:sport_id><s:story_id>59666</s:story_id></item><item><title>Mountaineers Capture Second Ranked Win of the Season for Second Time in Program History</title><link>https://wvusports.com/news/2026/11/8/volleyball-mountaineers-capture-second-ranked-win-of-the-season-for-second-time-in-program-history</link><guid>https://wvusports.com/news/2026/11/8/volleyball-mountaineers-capture-second-ranked-win-of-the-season-for-second-time-in-program-history</guid><category>Volleyball</category><description><![CDATA[<img alt="WVU Volleyball sings Country Roads following a 3-1 victory over No. 25 Colorado" src="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_primary&image_path=/images/2026/11/8/VB_WVUvsColorado_11-8_ECCOUNTRYRDS-2.jpg" /><br /><br />MORGANTOWN, W.Va. - The West Virginia University volleyball team (12-10, 5-7 Big 12) matched its single-season program record for ranked wins with a four-set victory over No. 25 Colorado on Sunday afternoon at Hope Coliseum, taking down the Buffaloes, 3-1, by set scores of 25-23, 23-25, 25-17 and 25-11.]]></description><media:thumbnail url="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_system&amp;image_path=/images/2026/11/8/VB_WVUvsColorado_11-8_ECCOUNTRYRDS-2.jpg" /><media:content url="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_primary&amp;image_path=/images/2026/11/8/VB_WVUvsColorado_11-8_ECCOUNTRYRDS-2.jpg"><media:title>WVU Volleyball sings Country Roads following a 3-1 victory over No. 25 Colorado</media:title></media:content><enclosure url="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_primary&amp;image_path=/images/2026/11/8/VB_WVUvsColorado_11-8_ECCOUNTRYRDS-2.jpg" length="1" type="image/jpg" /><pubDate>Sun, 8 Nov 2026 17:49:00 EST</pubDate><s:sport_id>17</s:sport_id><s:story_id>59665</s:story_id></item><item><title>No. 8-Seed WVU Set to Begin Play at 2026 Big 12 Tournament</title><link>https://wvusports.com/news/2026/11/8/womens-soccer-no-8-seed-wvu-set-to-begin-play-at-2026-big-12-tournament</link><guid>https://wvusports.com/news/2026/11/8/womens-soccer-no-8-seed-wvu-set-to-begin-play-at-2026-big-12-tournament</guid><category>Women's Soccer</category><description><![CDATA[<img alt="The WVU women's soccer team poses for a group photo at Texas Health Mansfield Stadium before the 2026 Big 12 Tournament." src="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_primary&image_path=/images/2026/11/8/Big_12_Tournament-20.jpg" /><br /><br />MANSFIELD, Texas – The West Virginia University women's soccer team opens postseason play at the 2026 Big 12 Soccer Tournament on Monday, Nov. 9, in Mansfield, Texas. The No. 8-seeded Mountaineers will take on No. 1-seed BYU at 3 p.m. ET/2 p.m. CT inside Texas Health Mansfield Stadium.]]></description><media:thumbnail url="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_system&amp;image_path=/images/2026/11/8/Big_12_Tournament-20.jpg" /><media:content url="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_primary&amp;image_path=/images/2026/11/8/Big_12_Tournament-20.jpg"><media:title>The WVU women's soccer team poses for a group photo at Texas Health Mansfield Stadium before the 2026 Big 12 Tournament.</media:title></media:content><enclosure url="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_primary&amp;image_path=/images/2026/11/8/Big_12_Tournament-20.jpg" length="1" type="image/jpg" /><pubDate>Sun, 8 Nov 2026 17:27:00 EST</pubDate><s:sport_id>13</s:sport_id><s:story_id>59664</s:story_id></item><item><title>WVU Rolls Past Georgia Tech on the Road</title><link>https://wvusports.com/news/2026/11/8/womens-basketball-wvu-rolls-past-georgia-tech-on-the-road</link><guid>https://wvusports.com/news/2026/11/8/womens-basketball-wvu-rolls-past-georgia-tech-on-the-road</guid><category>Women's Basketball</category><description><![CDATA[<img alt="Marya Hudgins celebrates the Mountaineers win over Georgia Tech" src="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_primary&image_path=/images/2026/11/8/THIRD_QUARTER_DW-18.jpg" /><br /><br />ATLANTA, Ga. – The No. 24 West Virginia women's basketball team improved to 3-0 on the season with an 81-63 road victory over Georgia Tech on Sunday afternoon at McCamish Pavilion.]]></description><media:thumbnail url="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_system&amp;image_path=/images/2026/11/8/THIRD_QUARTER_DW-18.jpg" /><media:content url="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_primary&amp;image_path=/images/2026/11/8/THIRD_QUARTER_DW-18.jpg"><media:title>Marya Hudgins celebrates the Mountaineers win over Georgia Tech</media:title></media:content><enclosure url="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_primary&amp;image_path=/images/2026/11/8/THIRD_QUARTER_DW-18.jpg" length="1" type="image/jpg" /><pubDate>Sun, 8 Nov 2026 16:23:00 EST</pubDate><s:sport_id>9</s:sport_id><s:story_id>59663</s:story_id></item><item><title>Ingleton, Nickel Highlight 2026 All-Big 12 Team Honors</title><link>https://wvusports.com/news/2026/11/8/womens-soccer-ingleton-nickel-highlight-2026-all-big-12-team-honors</link><guid>https://wvusports.com/news/2026/11/8/womens-soccer-ingleton-nickel-highlight-2026-all-big-12-team-honors</guid><category>Women's Soccer</category><description><![CDATA[<img alt="Nyema Ingleton and Sophia Nickel compete during home matches at Dick Dlesk Soccer Stadium." src="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_primary&image_path=/images/2026/11/8/Ny__Soph_2-up.png" /><br /><br />MANSFIELD, Texas – Four members of the West Virginia University women's soccer team have been named to the 2026 All-Big 12 Teams, the league announced on Sunday.]]></description><media:thumbnail url="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_system&amp;image_path=/images/2026/11/8/Ny__Soph_2-up.png" /><media:content url="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_primary&amp;image_path=/images/2026/11/8/Ny__Soph_2-up.png"><media:title>Nyema Ingleton and Sophia Nickel compete during home matches at Dick Dlesk Soccer Stadium.</media:title></media:content><enclosure url="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_primary&amp;image_path=/images/2026/11/8/Ny__Soph_2-up.png" length="1" type="image/jpg" /><pubDate>Sun, 8 Nov 2026 15:03:00 EST</pubDate><s:sport_id>13</s:sport_id><s:story_id>59662</s:story_id></item></channel></rss>